{"paper": "2024-Tier1-23-Sep-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential-count-mismatch", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 24, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The ratio of the ages of A and B, 3 years ago, was 5 : 7. The ratio of their ages, 13 years from now, will be 9 : 11. If the present age of C is 11 years less than that of B, then the present age of C, in years, is:", "options": [{"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Find the area of a rectangle whose length is 52m and breadth is 9m.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "495", "added": false}, {"text": "499", "added": false}, {"text": "510", "added": false}, {"text": "522", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The monthly production of electric bulbs by a company during the second half of the year 2021 is shown by the following bar graph. Study the bar graph carefully and answer the question given below. What is the percentage decrement in the production of electric bulbs in October as compared to the production in July? (Correct up to two decimal places.)", "options": [{"text": "30.28%", "added": false}, {"text": "31.82%", "added": false}, {"text": "29.82%", "added": false}, {"text": "32.28%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "In a team of seven members, the average age of six of the members is 42 years while the age of the seventh member of the team is 36 years more than the average age of all the seven members taken together. Find the age (in years) of the seventh member of the team.", "options": [{"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "84", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "78", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The sale of two kinds of bicycles B1 and B2 (in lakhs) manufactured by a company over a period of three years are shown in the table below. From 2001 to 2003, the total sale of bicycles B1 is what percent of the total sale of bicycles B2?", "options": [{"text": "70.6%", "added": false}, {"text": "68.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "62.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "56.7%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A class of 30 students appeared in a test. The average score of 12 students is 62, and that of the rest is 60. What is the average score of the class?", "options": [{"text": "58.8", "added": false}, {"text": "61.8", "added": false}, {"text": "60.8", "added": false}, {"text": "59.8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The length of the tangent drawn from a point 10 cm away from the centre of a circle with radius 4 cm, is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "If an employee's income is ₹72,000, the amount he spends is 40% higher than his savings. Therefore, his savings (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "30000", "added": false}, {"text": "34000", "added": false}, {"text": "32000", "added": false}, {"text": "28000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A customer pays ₹975 in instalments. The payment is done each month ₹5 less than the previous month. If the first instalment is ₹100, how much time will be taken to pay the entire amount?", "options": [{"text": "14 months", "added": false}, {"text": "15 months", "added": false}, {"text": "27 months", "added": false}, {"text": "26 months Q . 1 3 A 1. 5% n s", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Sequences and Series", "sub": "arithmetic-progression", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "If in a circle a chord of length 14 cm is at a distance of 24 cm from its centre, then the length of the radius of the circle is:", "options": [{"text": "28 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "31 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "25 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "37.5", "added": false}, {"text": "18.5", "added": false}, {"text": "60.5", "added": false}, {"text": "55.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "In ΔPQR, if 4∠ P = 5∠ Q = 20∠ R, then the value of ∠ Q is:", "options": [{"text": "72°", "added": false}, {"text": "36°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Two pipes A and B can fill a tank in 20 and 30 hours, respectively. Both pipes are opened to fill the tank, but when the tank is one-third full, a leak develops through which one-fourth of the water supplied by both pipes goes out. Find the total time (in hours) taken to fill the tank.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A boat covers a distance of 55 km downstream in 5 hours while it takes 11 hours to cover the same distance upstream. What is the speed of the boat?", "options": [{"text": "8 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "9 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "11 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "7 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "leak", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "The single discount equivalent to a series discount of 60%, 70% and 80%.", "options": [{"text": "97.6%", "added": false}, {"text": "70%", "added": false}, {"text": "85%", "added": false}, {"text": "95.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The number 4,29,714 is divisible by:", "options": [{"text": "3 and 5", "added": false}, {"text": "6 and 5", "added": false}, {"text": "4 and 6", "added": false}, {"text": "3 and 6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}]}